---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const APPLY_MAILTO =
  "mailto:earlyaccess@harborlauncher.com?subject=Harbor%20early%20access&body=Hi%2C%0A%0AOur%20studio%3A%20%0AOur%20game%20(Steam%20link)%3A%20%0AWhy%20we're%20interested%3A%20%0A";
---

<Base
  title="Early access · Harbor"
  description="Be one of the first developers shipping Harbor. Full launcher, six months free for accepted partners, and a direct line to the founder."
>
  <!-- ===== Hero ===== -->
  <section class="hero hero-page">
    <div class="dotgrid hero-grid"></div>
    <div class="container hero-inner">
      <span class="pill pill-teal" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
        <span class="pill-dot"></span>
        Design-partner program · limited spots
      </span>
      <h1 class="hero-headline" style="font-size:42px;line-height:1.12;">
        Own the launch,<br />
        keep the players,<br />
        be one of the first, with <span class="text-teal">Harbor</span>.
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-paragraph">
        We're onboarding a small group of studios to ship Harbor before launch. You get the full
        product and help shape it; we get honest feedback from people who actually run a live game.
        Accepted partners ship free for six months, and it's a real working relationship, not a beta list.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a href="#apply" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Apply to be a partner</a>
        <a href={APPLY_MAILTO} class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg">Email us directly</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== What you get ===== -->
  <section class="section section-ink">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">What you get</span>
        <h2 class="display-lg">The whole thing, not a trimmed-down trial.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Every partner ships the full launcher with all current modules. No feature gating during the program.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M3 9h18M8 14h5"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="card-title">The full launcher + every module</h3>
          <p class="card-body">White-label launcher with email capture, patch notes, news, and surveys. All of it, branded to your game. New modules land in your build as we ship them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 2"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="card-title">Six months free</h3>
          <p class="card-body">Accepted partners pay nothing for the first six months. No card, no invoice. You're helping us get it right; that's the deal.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon neutral">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 12a8 8 0 0 1 16 0"/><path d="M2 12h2M20 12h2M12 2v2"/><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="card-title">CDN delivery, handled</h3>
          <p class="card-body">Your launcher and its content are served from a global CDN, so patch notes and news land fast wherever your players are. We run the infrastructure; you don't think about it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon neutral">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 15a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7l-4 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="card-title">A direct line to the founder</h3>
          <p class="card-body">You're not filing tickets into a void. The founder building Harbor is on the other end for setup, requests, and the occasional 11pm "can it do this?"</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout neutral" style="margin-top:44px;">
        <span class="callout-icon">
          <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"/></svg>
        </span>
        <p class="callout-body"><strong>Worried it might break a storefront rule?</strong> Harbor takes no payments, runs no ads, and never modifies your game. Here's exactly what it does and doesn't do. <a href="/tos-compliance" class="text-teal" style="text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px;">Read the storefront-transparency page →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== Pricing ===== -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head center">
        <span class="eyebrow">After the free window</span>
        <h2 class="display-lg">Simple, flat pricing.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Free for accepted partners for six months. After that, plans start at $40/mo, with
          advanced modules on the Pro tier.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flat-price">
        <div class="flat-price-amount"><span class="from">From</span>$40<span class="per"> / mo, per game</span></div>
        <p class="flat-price-sub">
          Flat SaaS pricing per game. <strong>No revenue share, no cut of your sales, ever.</strong>
          We'll talk pricing well before month six; no surprise bill.
        </p>
        <ul class="flat-price-list">
          <li><span class="price-check"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg></span><span><strong>No revenue share</strong>: a flat subscription, never a percentage</span></li>
          <li><span class="price-check"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg></span><span><strong>Email capture included</strong> on every plan</span></li>
          <li><span class="price-check"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg></span><span><strong>Surveys and analytics</strong> on the Pro tier</span></li>
          <li><span class="price-check"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg></span><span><strong>Six months free</strong> for accepted partners</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== Apply / email CTA ===== -->
  <section class="cta-band" id="apply">
    <div class="dotgrid cta-band-grid"></div>
    <div class="container cta-band-inner" style="max-width:680px;">
      <span class="eyebrow">Come on as a partner</span>
      <h2 class="display-lg" style="margin-bottom:16px;">Email us. Tell us about your game.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom:30px;">One line about your studio and your Steam page is plenty. If it's a fit, we'll set up a short call and get you shipping. No forms, no funnel.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a href={APPLY_MAILTO} class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
          <svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="m3 7 9 6 9-6"/></svg>
          earlyaccess@harborlauncher.com
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="form-note">We read every email and reply within a couple of days.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .flat-price {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: var(--harbor-ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--teal-border);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    padding: 36px 40px;
  }
  .flat-price-amount {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 44px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .flat-price-amount .from {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text2);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-right: 8px;
  }
  .flat-price-amount .per {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text3);
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }
  .flat-price-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text2);
    margin: 10px 0 0;
  }
  .flat-price-sub strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .flat-price-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    padding: 20px 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--harbor-line);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 14px 24px;
  }
  .flat-price-list li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text2);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .flat-price-list .price-check {
    color: var(--teal);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .flat-price-list strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .flat-price {
      padding: 26px 22px;
    }
    .flat-price-list {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Fire a PostHog conversion event for the early-access view (production only;
  // window.posthog is absent in dev/preview, so it's optional-chained).
  window.posthog?.capture('early_access_view');
</script>
